  "intro": {
    "copy": "How do you turn a much-loved local food business into a brand ready to travel? For this Sydney-based empanada company, the answer was hiding in the pastry. We renamed Copetín as Coptown and built the identity around the repulgue, the traditional hand-crimped edge of an empanada. Its distinctive form became both the letter C and a playful wave, bringing a little Sydney surf culture into the mix. Different crimps, colours and characters give every flavour its own personality.",
    "title": "Coptown",
    "subtitle": "An empanada that learned to surf.",
    "services": [
      "Visual Identity",
      "Art Direction",
      "Branding"
    ]
  },
